I'd put all of it in one `routing.toml` and keep no routing facts in the code.

**Why the files drift:** `apply_payments_override` keeps its own copies of two facts the CSVs already hold. `FINANCE_SERVICES` is exactly the set of services `billing` owns, and `URGENT` is exactly the set of severities whose channel is `page`. Several ordinary edits therefore break the override without anyone seeing it. A new billing service wouldn't get the override. Setting sev3 to `page` wouldn't trigger it. Moving `payments` to another team would still send its urgent alerts to finance.

**What I'd change:**

```toml
[channels]
sev1 = "page"
sev2 = "page"
sev3 = "slack"
sev4 = "email"

[owners]
checkout      = { team = "storefront" }
search        = { team = "discovery" }
catalog       = { team = "discovery" }
payments      = { team = "billing", pages_to = "finance-oncall" }
ledger        = { team = "billing", pages_to = "finance-oncall" }
notifications = { team = "platform" }
auth          = { team = "identity" }
inventory     = { team = "fulfilment" }
shipping      = { team = "fulfilment" }
```

- `route()` looks up the channel and the owner. If the channel is `page` and the owner has `pages_to`, it uses that team. `FINANCE_SERVICES`, `URGENT` and `apply_payments_override` are deleted, and the escalation sits on the same line as the owner it overrides.
- The two CSVs are replaced by this file, and the README is updated to match. `tomllib` is in the standard library on your Python 3.14.
- Routing results stay the same. All of September's services and severities are covered, and the override changed the route for 22 alerts (sev1/sev2 on `payments` and `ledger`).

**One thing to settle first:** the docstring says urgent money-path alerts page finance on-call "as well as the owner". The code replaces `billing` with `finance-oncall` instead, so billing never saw those 22 alerts. If finance is meant to be paged in addition to billing, `route()` has to return more than one team, which changes its return shape. If replacing billing is intended, the design above works as written and only the docstring is wrong. Which do you want?

